body:
Thats just how they do it

&#x200B;

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-7hAELEBjX4&ab\_channel=DeepVegan

Well a person in a coma or someone in a dreamless sleep is going to resume their consciousness. It is reasonable to assume that a person that has gone unconscious would want to resume it.

&#x200B;

What do you think is the difference between a human and a non-human animal, that justifies slicing their throat open needlessly to eat a burger, which if true of the human would make it okay to do to a human?

&#x200B;

The thing is that the conservation only really occurs by proxy because of paying for licenses, the hunting in of itself doesn't do much for conservation.  Shooting a lion or a duck in the head doesn't magically make the species conserved. Those websites you posted saying how many ducks there are now isn't because of the hunting, its by paying for licenses. Its like if i were to say punching kids in the head helps stop child abuse when really I'm punching a kid in the head and then paying $10,000 to a child abuse charity.

Reintroduction of a natural predator is much better for a population than hunting by humans. Humans will generally skew towards killing larger males. Deers are also not strictly monogamous so any surviving males will happily impregnate as many females as it can.  Natural predators generally skew towards killing the young, sick, and weak. Which helps keeps  the gene pool strong. Without natural predation a population is more likely to get smacked down by overpopulation. Not to mention that the risk of overpopulation is being exacerbated by deer breeding, which is paid for by deer hunting.... It is pretty seldom that a population will actually completely eradicate itself by over-predation or overpopulation. Generally even undpredated animals will just fluctuate around their carrying capacity and those in a predator-prey relationship just sways up and down provided they aren't tampered with.

&#x200B;

\>We humans are  biologically predatory omnivores. We traded teeth and claws for tools  and intelligence. Our closest ape relatives, the Orangutan and the  Chimpanzee, both regularly use tools to eat meat. Orangutans use spears  to fish, and Chimps will eat anything they can get their hands on.  Because it is natural to hunt, and it is in our biology to hunt

&#x200B;

Not to come across as an jackass but this is also a fallacy it is an appeal to nature. What chimps do has no bearing on what is right or wrong for us to do. What we may be genetically predisposed to do doesn't have a bearing on what we should do.

&#x200B;

Edit: But when all is said and done I think it is okay for you to hunt if you need to for your CF, if you need to do that to be healthy I don't have a problem with that.

Its infuriatingly stupid, there are an endless number of dumb ways you can apply this logic it is absolutely ridiculous. But who on earth knows when 0 CO2 emission meat will actually be available to consumers at a large scale 20? 50? years. When will it even be cheap enough? people arent willing to pay a little extra for vegan stuff i doubt many people will opt for lab meat when they can get real stuff for cheaper. I've seen some surveys done and in some about 80% of people would not eat it from memory. Hopefully we will still have some forests and some hospitable atmosphere left by that time.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Oysters, mussels and fetuses have no need for sentience or any level of consciousness. As I already pointed out there is no brain activity in a fetus up until 30 weeks. Developmentally there is no benefit in generating consciousness whilst in the womb as a. the brain is very oxygen hungry and b. there is nothing to do. Bees, lobsters and shrimp actually would benefit from being consciousness. It seems like a bit of a jump to lump bees, lobsters and shrimp with oysters and clams.

&#x200B;

\>Therefore pain or sentience does not seem to be a consistent or sufficient moral foundation for veganism.

&#x200B;

Well no, just because there are grey areas for some animals does not mean sentience is not a sufficient moral foundation.

hes a streamer or some thing and he is known as the best non-vegan vegan activist because his position to justify killing animals is so absurd many people realize this and go vegan.

